Design for  Non-Destructive Disassembly or Demanufacturing strategy gives a better chance to product to be disassembled into different elements for major remanufacturing quality. This strategy can be used for different reasons: as a maintenance activity (to swap one part for another one to be reused, clean, repaired, refurbished or resold component and materials), recycling operation or dispose of hazardous materials. In this strategy, the sequence of disassembling tasks and operations must be set up logically in order to facilitate and faster the disassembling process. Depending on product typology, the disassembling ca be performed using an automatic or human disassembling process. To facilitate the human disassembling process it is necessary to use basic hand tools to reduce labour costs.

Disassembling generates significant economic benefits for communities while reducing the need for new landfills, preventing pollution, saving energy, and reducing greenhouse gas emissions. The disassembling process employs low-, medium-, and highly-skilled workers in a variety of jobs—from handling and refining to delivering high-quality goods. Further, these jobs will often require high mobility as they are embodied in a global market.